# OSD/OS's changes to RetroArch 1.20.0 (commit
# ab3b175848fa6cd8b2340809631e30bc0fe1d136, the v1.20.0 tag), which
# scripts/build-retroarch.sh applies before it builds the Linux arm64
# package's RetroArch. Each part, with where it comes from:
#
# 1. network/netplay/netplay_frontend.c, netplay_handshake_pre_sync() and
#    the NETPLAY_CMD_MODE case of netplay_get_cmd(): the joining side
#    refuses a client number the host sends that is out of range, or that
#    is not its own in a mode change addressed to it, before it indexes
#    its per-client arrays with it. Upstream 9a19e7a94d4891657d1d57f61f69c5aec317343d
#    ("netplay: validate assigned client number before use"), ported by
#    hand: 1.20.0 keeps the host's pause as netplay->remote_paused where
#    master has NETPLAY_FLAG_REMOTE_PAUSED.
# 2. input/input_driver.c, input_remote_init_network(): the network
#    gamepad's UDP socket is bound to 127.0.0.1 instead of every address,
#    so that only this machine can press its buttons. OSD/OS's own.
# 3. libretro-common/streams/file_stream.c, filestream_vscanf(): an
#    out-of-bounds read through an uninitialised length (CVE-2025-9136).
#    Upstream b0999db885a0f1530f0e968c7450a4f0aa624b65 ("properly
#    initialize variable (#17555)").
# 4. network/netplay/netplay_frontend.c, netplay_handle_slaves(): a NULL
#    dereference when a frame's input is replayed. Upstream
#    8fd7aa48c61891aa93f995e4e04bdf50a57a6677 ("network/netplay/netplay_frontend:
#    NULL-check istate_out in frame real_input copy path").
# 5. deps/bearssl-0.6 (BearSSL 0.6, RetroArch's TLS here): a CBC record
#    whose length is not a whole number of blocks is refused
#    (src/ssl/ssl_rec_cbc.c), and the X.509 and private-key decoders stop
#    at their first error (src/x509/). BearSSL upstream
#    7bea48e5e850ab4cafbe68d3765cdaba13a86d6f ("Fixed bug in handling
#    incoming records with invalid length") and
#    3479195d052cc59db5358730ff3ad829abb7aced ("Fixed chunked decoding in
#    case of errors"), from https://www.bearssl.org/git/BearSSL, with
#    their paths under deps/bearssl-0.6.
#
# None of it changes RetroArch's version, its netplay protocol or what two
# machines send each other: a RetroArch built with it plays with a stock
# 1.20.0. Made on 2026-11-25 with git diff against the tag; applied with
# patch -p1.

diff --git a/deps/bearssl-0.6/src/ssl/ssl_rec_cbc.c b/deps/bearssl-0.6/src/ssl/ssl_rec_cbc.c
index c080604..2ae3558 100644
--- a/deps/bearssl-0.6/src/ssl/ssl_rec_cbc.c
+++ b/deps/bearssl-0.6/src/ssl/ssl_rec_cbc.c
@@ -70,7 +70,7 @@ cbc_check_length(const br_sslrec_in_cbc_context *cc, size_t rlen)
 		min_len += blen;
 		max_len += blen;
 	}
-	return min_len <= rlen && rlen <= max_len;
+	return min_len <= rlen && rlen <= max_len && (rlen & (blen - 1)) == 0;
 }
 
